1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,002
Welcome. This short walkthrough takes you from machine
readiness and Azure portal setup

2
00:00:05,002 --> 00:00:10,004
to running Edge RAG and testing two questions. Setup is
illustrated step by

3
00:00:10,004 --> 00:00:12,697
step, followed by actual recorded query results.

4
00:00:14,708 --> 00:00:19,969
Use a compatible x64 Windows workstation or virtual machine.
Plan sixteen virtual CPUs,

5
00:00:19,969 --> 00:00:25,229
ninety six to one hundred twenty eight gibibytes of host
memory, and about

6
00:00:25,229 --> 00:00:30,489
sixty four for Docker. Reserve at least one hundred fifty
gibibytes of free

7
00:00:30,489 --> 00:00:35,750
persistent storage for initial downloads. Confirm Linux
containers, the Docker server, and x64

8
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:36,963
Python before continuing.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,034
In Azure portal, select Create a resource and search for
Azure AI Language.

10
00:00:44,034 --> 00:00:49,069
Choose your subscription, resource group, approved region,
unique name, and a tier supported

11
00:00:49,069 --> 00:00:54,103
by the selected containers. Review and create. After
deployment, open Keys and Endpoint

12
00:00:54,103 --> 00:00:57,201
privately and securely save the endpoint and key.

13
00:00:59,208 --> 00:01:04,562
Next, create a Document Intelligence resource. Complete the
same subscription, resource group, region,

14
00:01:04,562 --> 00:01:09,915
name, and pricing tier steps. Deploy it and securely obtain
its own endpoint

15
00:01:09,915 --> 00:01:15,268
and key. Confirm that your organization permits the
container billing authentication and required

16
00:01:15,268 --> 00:01:17,739
outbound connections before starting the lab.

17
00:01:19,750 --> 00:01:24,502
Clone Edge RAG into a new folder and select the workshop
release shown.

18
00:01:24,502 --> 00:01:29,254
Create the x64 Python environment, install the listed lab
dependencies, and run pip

19
00:01:29,254 --> 00:01:34,006
check. Keep the Qdrant client below version one point
sixteen. You can copy

20
00:01:34,006 --> 00:01:37,296
the full commands from the published partner enablement
guide.

21
00:01:39,333 --> 00:01:43,810
Prepare B G E M three and Qwen two point five using a

22
00:01:43,810 --> 00:01:48,287
working host Ollama installation, or reuse approved
downloaded models. Confirm both models are

23
00:01:48,287 --> 00:01:52,764
present and point to their populated directory. The
demonstration uses a separate Ollama

24
00:01:52,764 --> 00:01:55,174
container on port eleven four three five.

25
00:01:57,208 --> 00:02:02,631
Save a private dot env file with the two Azure resource
endpoints, billing

26
00:02:02,631 --> 00:02:08,055
URLs, keys, and model directory. Replace the illustrated
placeholders, use plain URLs, and

27
00:02:08,055 --> 00:02:13,478
keep the cloud billing addresses. The launcher selects local
inference automatically. Verify that

28
00:02:13,478 --> 00:02:17,649
Git ignores dot env, and never share the actual keys.

29
00:02:19,667 --> 00:02:25,734
Validate Compose with config quiet, start the stack, and
check that all eight

30
00:02:25,734 --> 00:02:31,801
containers are running. Then run the service verifier. It
exercises actual Language processing,

31
00:02:31,801 --> 00:02:36,468
PDF extraction, embeddings, and generation. Continue when
every check passes.

32
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:43,135
For a fresh lab, index the English sample documents once.
Expect eight chunks,

33
00:02:43,135 --> 00:02:47,771
then run the verifier with dash dash rag. Start the
interface with the

34
00:02:47,771 --> 00:02:52,406
supplied launcher and open localhost port eighty five zero
three on the same

35
00:02:52,406 --> 00:02:57,041
host. In a VM lab, use the browser inside the VM. Skip
indexing

36
00:02:57,041 --> 00:02:59,180
if the collection is already populated.

37
00:03:01,208 --> 00:03:06,432
Here is the actual recorded query workflow. Keep B G E M
three

38
00:03:06,432 --> 00:03:11,656
and the Qwen generator selected, choose the business
partnership filter, and enter the

39
00:03:11,656 --> 00:03:16,880
investment question. Select Enhanced Search and Generate.
The recorded answer identifies Microsoft's investment

40
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:22,103
as one point five billion dollars. Expand Source One to
inspect the supporting

41
00:03:22,103 --> 00:03:25,318
partnership text. The investment amount matches the
document.

42
00:03:47,083 --> 00:03:52,078
For the second question, ask which cloud platform G42 will
use for its

43
00:03:52,078 --> 00:03:57,074
AI services. Submit it through the same Streamlit interface.
The recorded answer identifies

44
00:03:57,074 --> 00:04:02,069
Microsoft's Azure cloud platform. Open a retrieved source
and compare that key fact

45
00:04:02,069 --> 00:04:07,064
with the partnership document. These two examples show local
retrieval and generation working

46
00:04:07,064 --> 00:04:10,138
together, with source evidence available in the interface.

47
00:04:34,042 --> 00:04:38,662
You are ready to rehearse: confirm the host, configure the
Azure resources, start

48
00:04:38,662 --> 00:04:43,283
and validate the containers, then run the sample questions
and inspect their sources.

49
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:47,548
Keep the partner enablement guide open for the full commands
and troubleshooting.
